# Project coding standards

## General

- Do not add obvious comments. Comment only non-obvious intent or constraints.
- Follow sibling files for structure and naming; prefer reuse over new abstractions.
- Run `vendor/bin/pint --dirty --format agent` after PHP edits.
- Prefer feature tests (`php artisan make:test --phpunit`) over one-off tinker scripts. Factories beyond `UserFactory` often need creating from scratch — mirror Action validation when testing.

## PHP

- Prefer `match` over `switch`.
- Use constructor property promotion; omit empty constructors.
- Declare return types; import classes with `use` (do not FQCN inline unless matching nearby style).
- Use Laravel helpers when available: `auth()->id()`, `redirect()->route()`, `fake()` in factories — not Facade imports solely for those calls.

## Laravel structure (v11+/v12)

- No new service providers unless necessary; register in `bootstrap/providers.php`.
- Schedule in `routes/console.php`. Middleware aliases in `bootstrap/app.php`. Reference middleware by class on routes when possible.
- Form Requests for controller validation; slim controllers; domain logic in Actions (see actions-handlers rule).
- Pivot table names: alphabetical (`project_role`, not `role_project`).
- Policies are auto-discovered.
- Eloquent lifecycle: this app uses `$dispatchesEvents`, model `booted`, and payment **handlers** — not attribute-based Observers. Prefer those existing patterns for billing side effects.
- Local URL (Herd): `http://wemx.test`.

## Livewire / Volt

- New Livewire UI must be **Volt single-file components** inside the admin/client theme trees (see themes-ui rule), not class components under `app/Livewire` unless matching an existing exception.
